# Lychee URL ignore list (regex per line).
# Used by .github/workflows/ci.yml `links` job to suppress known-noisy
# externals (e.g. rate-limited LinkedIn, archive.org, social hosts) so
# they don't fail the run. Internal 4xx/5xx still fail.

# Self-references in canonical URLs / OG tags / sitemap / RSS / Atom.
# These are absolute URLs to the production host; pre-deploy the site
# isn't live, and post-deploy lychee resolves them against dist/ via
# --root-dir already. Skipping the network round-trip avoids both
# false-negatives pre-deploy and rate-limited self-hits post-deploy.
^https://ryanhenderson\.dev/

# Test-fixture projects with intentionally-fake repoUrls. alpha exercises
# the active-project repo-button path; charlie exercises the archived
# variant. Real projects (butverify, c3p, pearl) point at real repos and
# are checked normally.
^https://github\.com/htxryan/(alpha|charlie)$
